MODEL DISCLAIMER
----------------
The simulation numbers, latencies, utilisation figures and throughput shown in
this project are ILLUSTRATIVE and scaled to make the architecture observable.
They are a teaching model, not measurements or benchmarks of any MongoDB
deployment. Do not cite them as sizing guidance. The four WiredTiger eviction
thresholds, the default cache-size rule, the 9.0 per-operation memory limit
and the 9.0 transaction cap are quoted from MongoDB's public documentation
(see docs/verification.md); everything else is invented for legibility.

The optional "Measured server" panel reports numbers read from a real
`serverStatus` document on a MongoDB you run yourself. Those are separately
labelled measurements and are never fed into the illustrative model.

